title: Hello
color: blue
position: -36,-75
---
<<if not visited("Hello")>>
Alchemy. What a theme. Am I right? How to represent a protoscientific school of hermetic wisdom? Okay, let's try the four elements.
<<set $earth = 0>>
<<set $water = 0>>
<<set $fire = 0>>
<<set $air = 0>>
<<else>>
<<set $ch = random_range(0, 5)>>
Four elements.
<<if $ch == 0>>
I know. It's not really alchemy. But atomic elements hadn't been discovered yet!
<<elseif $ch == 1>>
Style, form, diction, flow?
<<elseif $ch == 2>>
Bools, numbers, strings, functions?
<<endif>>
<<endif>>
-> Water
  <<if $water == 0>>
  <<set $water_level = 0.5>>
  <<set $water_ball_count = 10>>
  <<set $water_ball_size = 0.25>>
  <<else>>
  <<set $water_level = $water_level + 0.25>>
  <<set $water_ball_count = $water_ball_count + 10>>
  <<set $water_ball_size = $water_ball_size * 1.25>>
  <<endif>>
  <<if $water == 0>>
  Water is wet.
  <<elseif $water == 1>>
  Splash.
  <<elseif $water == 2>>
  It's water.
  <<elseif $water == 3>>
  "Aqua vitae" is not water! It's grain alcohol!
  <<elseif $water == 4>>
  We'll keep doing this.
  <<elseif $water >= 5>>
  ...
  <<endif>>
  <<set $water = $water + 1>>
  <<attach_script_3 "water" {$water_level} {$water_ball_count} {$water_ball_size}>>
-> Earth
  <<declare $cube_size = 0.5 as number>>
  <<if $earth == 0>>
  <<set $cube_size = 0.5>>
  Do cubes count?
  <<set $earth = $earth + 1>>
  <<attach_script_5 "earth" 5 5 0 {$cube_size} Glass>>
  <<elseif $earth == 1>>
  How about a lot of cubes?
  <<set $earth = $earth + 1>>
  <<set $cube_size to 0.75>>
  <<attach_script_5 "earth" 5 10 0 {$cube_size} Wood>>
  <<else>>
  <<if $earth < 3>>
  How about just *too many* cubes?
  <<set $earth = $earth + 1>>
  <<set $cube_size = 1.0>>
  <<set $mat = "Stone">>
  <<else>>
  I'm out of ideas.
  <<set $mat = "Sand">>
  <<set $cube_size = $cube_size + 0.25>>
  <<endif>>
  <<attach_script_5 "earth" {random_range(5,7)} {random_range(10,13)} {random_range(3,5)} {$cube_size} {$mat}>>
  <<endif>>
-> Air
  <<if $air == 0>>
  Air, that source of inspiration.
  Um.
  I don't have a gas simulation, but you know, a lot of gas was huffed in alchemists' labs.
  OK, gravity. That happens in the air.
  <<set $air_count = 100>>
  <<elseif $air == 1>>
  Boring? I guess.
  <<elseif $air == 2>>
  Even more?
  <<elseif $air == 3>>
  If things slow down, gotta start over.
  <<else>>
  ...
  <<endif>>
  <<set $air = $air + 1>>
  <<attach_script_3 "air" {$air_count} 0.2 1.0e4>>
  <<set $air_count = $air_count + 100>>
-> Fire
    <<if $fire == 0>>
    Fire, fire... no time for integrating Hanabi...
    You heard about cats and dogs?
    Look at these two. They can't get along.
    <<elseif $fire == 1>>
    Did you see that?
    <<elseif $fire == 2>>
    These animals are like oil and water.
    (What element is oil? Water plus earth?)
    <<elseif $fire == 3>>
    Are you seeing this?
    <<elseif $fire == 4>>
    They just go to pieces.
    <<else>>
    ...
    <<endif>>
    <<set $fire = $fire + 1>>
    <<set $x = -7.5 + ($fire * 3) % 7>>
    <<set $z = -9.0 + ($fire * 5) % 11>>
    <<attach_script_4 "fire" {$x} 0.1 {$z} {random_range(40.0, 70.0)}>>
-> (leave)
===
